Conditions run code only when something is true.
if marks >= 40: print("pass")
elif marks >= 35: print("grace")
else: print("fail")
Indentation (4 spaces) is required.

OOP organises code into classes (blueprints) and objects (instances). Four pillars: Encapsulation, Abstraction, Inheritance, Polymorphism.
class Dog:
    def __init__(self, name):
        self.name = name
`self` refers to the current object.

Recursion is a function calling itself, and it needs a base case to stop.
def fact(n):
    return 1 if n <= 1 else n * fact(n - 1)
Dynamic programming stores sub-results (memoization) to avoid repeated work.
